# Admin Content Sync

When an admin adds or edits content from `owner-projects.html`, it must appear on the matching public page via the API.

## Data flow

- **Feedback**: admin POST `/api/admin/feedback` → public GET `/api/feedback` → render in `#feedbackCards` on `index.html` via `feedback.js`
- **Projects**: admin POST `/api/admin/projects` → public GET `/api/projects` → render in `#projectsGrid` on `projects.html` via `projects.js`

## Rules

- Public pages always load from the API; never rely on hardcoded placeholder cards in HTML.
- After admin create/update/delete, call `notifyPublicRefresh("vidyut-feedback-refresh")` or `notifyPublicRefresh("vidyut-projects-refresh")` so open public tabs reload.
- `feedback.js` and `projects.js` must define `escapeHtml` before rendering API data.
- Do not duplicate public render logic inside `owner-projects.js`; keep admin page focused on forms and admin lists.

## Example

```javascript
// owner-projects.js — after successful admin write
notifyPublicRefresh("vidyut-feedback-refresh");

// feedback.js — homepage listens and reloads
window.addEventListener("storage", (event) => {
  if (event.key === "vidyut-feedback-refresh") loadFeedbackCards();
});
```
